# M-panic-location, panel 230's R1, kind 2: a C handle given back that the
# program never held names the call that gave it back. `g_open` is `borrows`, so
# no life of the program's began, and the first `g_close` is refused before C,
# at the place where it begins; the second is never reached. The header and the
# program are `fixedbugs-a-double-release-before-any-acquisition-is-stopped-before-c`'s.

extern "fixedbugs-a-double-release-before-any-acquisition-is-stopped-before-c.h"
    record G tag gg
    function g_open() -> G borrows
    function g_close(x: G consumes)

function main()
    a = g_open()
    print("opened")
    twice = a
    g_close(x: a)
    g_close(x: twice)
    print("closed twice")
